\title{gamRTMB: distributional regression with mgcv smooths and RTMB}
\description{
Fits GAMLSS-style models in which every parameter of a distribution may
carry smooth terms. The pieces are borrowed rather than rebuilt:
\pkg{mgcv} constructs the bases and penalties, \code{\link[mgcv:smooth2random]{mgcv::smooth2random()}}
turns the penalized coefficients into iid Gaussian random effects,
\pkg{RTMB} supplies automatic differentiation and the Laplace
approximation, and \pkg{RTMBdist} supplies the log-densities in each
distribution's own native parameterisation.
}
\section{Entry points}{

\code{\link[=gamRTMB]{gamRTMB()}} fits a model, \code{\link[=rtmbdist_family]{rtmbdist_family()}} builds a family object from
any suitable RTMBdist density, and \code{\link[=edf]{edf()}} reports effective degrees of
freedom per smooth.
}

